From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:56:11 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] ps1-tests

The PS1 memory card survives a restart byte for byte: a 128 KB card on
the SD card reaches pcsx at boot, comes back out on eject, and is the
card the next session's game sees. A GBA game played after a PS1 game
gets the same input (triggers, Select+X, pass-through) and the same
picture (source rect, frame width, 240x160 frame) as a GBA-only run.
ps1_analog forces pcsx_rearmed_bios=HLE like the other direct-core tests.
